small following and zero ad spend. Start growing a list that actually 
converts.]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="sqsrte-large">Written by <a href="https://www.chloeleonard.com/chloe-leonard">Chloe Leonard</a>, Founder of CL Studio</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">If you have been told that growing an email list requires a big social following or a significant ad budget, I want to offer you a different perspective. Some of the most engaged, high-converting email lists were built with neither of those things. What they were built with was<strong> a clear value proposition, a smart lead magnet, and a consistent strategy </strong>for turning website visitors and social followers into subscribers.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Your email list is one of the few marketing assets you actually own. Social media platforms change their algorithms and their rules constantly, but your email list belongs to <em>you</em>. When you want to reach your audience, you reach them directly, without paying for the privilege and without competing for attention in a crowded feed.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Here is how to grow it quickly, without spending a dollar on ads.</p>


  









<hr />
  
    
  
  <h2 data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_28477">Start with a Lead Magnet Worth Signing Up For</h2><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">The fastest way to grow an email list is to give people a compelling reason to join it. A generic "sign up for updates" prompt is not going to move the needle these days. People need to feel like they are getting something valuable in exchange for their email address.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">A lead magnet can take a lot of forms depending on your business: a free guide, a checklist, a template, a mini course, a quiz with personalized results, a discount code, a free resource download, or access to exclusive content.<strong> The best lead magnets are specific, immediately useful, and directly relevant to the problem your ideal customer is trying to solve.</strong></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">For example, if you are a <a href="https://www.chloeleonard.com/branding-agency-for-small-business">branding agency for small business</a> owners, a <span data-text-attribute-id="f8e17a5f-5d8e-4903-a2fc-687d37eeb0d9" class="sqsrte-text-highlight"><a target="_blank" href="https://clstudio.myflodesk.com/brandaudit">free brand audit checklist</a></span> like the one we have would be an incredibly relevant and useful lead magnet. Someone who downloads that is already telling you they care about their brand, which means they are a warm lead from the moment they subscribe.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">If you are an e-commerce brand, a discount code of 15% or higher or early access offer tends to convert well. If you are a service provider, a guide that answers a question your ideal client is always asking is a strong starting point.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true"><strong>The key is specificity. </strong>The more targeted the lead magnet is to a particular person with a particular problem, the higher your conversion rate will be.</p><h2 data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Optimize Every Page of Your Website for Sign Ups</h2>


  




















































  

    
  
    

      

      
