  <p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23596">If your email opt-in only lives in the footer of your website, you are leaving a lot of subscribers on the table. Think about every page of your site as an opportunity to invite someone onto your list.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23583"><strong>The most effective placements for email opt-ins are:</strong></p><ul data-rte-list="default" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23584"><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">a pop-up that triggers after someone has been on the page for thirty seconds or has scrolled sixty percent of the way down</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">an inline form embedded within your blog posts</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">a dedicated landing page for your lead magnet that you can link to directly</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">a sticky header or announcement bar with a clear call to action.</p></li></ul><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23585">You do not need all of these at once so pick two or three that feel right for your site and test them. A well-placed opt-in form with a strong lead magnet can convert a meaningful percentage of your existing website traffic into subscribers, without changing anything else about your marketing.</p><h2 data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23586">Use Your Social Media Strategically</h2><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23587">A massive social following is not necessary to grow your list, as long as you are intentional about directing the audience you do have toward your email opt-in.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23588"><strong>A few ways to do this effectively: </strong></p><ul data-rte-list="default" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23589"><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">add your lead magnet link to your Instagram bio and reference it regularly in your content,</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">create posts or reels that preview the value of your lead magnet and prompt people to grab it</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">use Stories to share snippets of your email content so followers understand what they are missing</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">pin a post about your lead magnet to the top of your profile where it is easy to find</p></li></ul><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23590">The mistake most people make is posting their lead magnet once and moving on. Treat it like a permanent part of your content rotation and mention it regularly in different ways.</p><h2 data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23591">Collaborate to Reach New Audiences</h2><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23592">One of the fastest ways to grow your email list is to get in front of someone else's audience. Collaboration does not require paid partnerships or a massive platform. It just requires finding people who serve a similar audience without directly competing with you.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23593">Guest blogging on a relevant website, being a guest on a podcast your ideal clients listen to, co-hosting a webinar or Instagram Live with a complementary brand, or doing a newsletter swap with another small business owner are all ways to introduce yourself to a new audience and direct them to your opt-in.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1779483489161_23594">At CL Studio, we work with small business owners across Nashville and beyond as a <span data-text-attribute-id="6e1c430d-fe5e-4096-bd40-7c5da0fa5a5a" class="sqsrte-text-highlight"><a href="https://www.chloeleonard.com/creative-agency-for-small-business">creative agency for small business</a></span> growth, and collaboration is one of the strategies we see consistently underused. It costs nothing except a little time and relationship building, and the results can be significant.</p>


  




















































  

    
  
    

      

      
